          "title": "Reach For Native First",
          "text": "`INCR`, `SETNX`, `GETSET`, `SET k v NX EX 30`, `LMOVE`, `ZADD GT` — one command beats any construct."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SET key val NX EX ttl` replaces the old `SETNX`+`EXPIRE` pair",
            "That pair had a crash-between-commands bug; the single form has none"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lua vs WATCH"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Lua wins when",
                "lines": [
                  "key is hot / contended",
                  "correctness critical",
                  "check + write inseparable"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "WATCH wins when",
                "lines": [
                  "computation is expensive",
                  "needs an external API",
                  "heavy math client-side"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lua under contention: no retries, no wasted RTTs, no livelock",
            "One pass, always succeeds — the server does the branching"
          ]
        }
      ]
